From 3c1f9a4d2b7e5081a6c4f0d9e3b275aa41c8f6d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhugengyu <zhugengyu2023@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Oct 2026 04:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(port/ehci): poll for the iaa handshake instead of spinning
 on it

usbh_kill_urb() waits for the IAA interrupt to finish its handshake by
spinning on qh->killed with a bound counted in loop iterations (200000 of
them).  Two things are wrong with that: the wait burns the core for its
whole duration although the killer is a thread that could sleep, and the
bound is not a time - how long 200000 iterations take is whatever the
compiler and the clock made of the loop, so the timeout this path
documents is not the timeout it has.

Spin for the first rounds (the controller raises the IAA as soon as it has
retired the descriptor, so the common case leaves the loop at once) and
then sleep one tick between checks.  The budget becomes rounds plus naps,
which is a real time bound, and a handshake that never completes no longer
costs a core.

The wait stays in thread context: every caller of usbh_kill_urb() is a
class driver's teardown or a host controller kill, never an interrupt
handler.

Signed-off-by: zhugengyu <zhugengyu2023@gmail.com>
---
 port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c | 44 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)
--- a/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c	2026-10-17 04:37:38.598413365 +0800
+++ b/port/ehci/usb_hc_ehci.c	2026-10-17 04:37:38.601085214 +0800
@@ -1423,24 +1423,36 @@
         EHCI_HCOR->usbcmd |= EHCI_USBCMD_IAAD;
         usb_osal_leave_critical_section(flags);
 
-        volatile uint32_t timeout = 0;
+        /*
+         * Wait for the IAA to finish the handshake.  The interrupt is
+         * normally imminent - the controller raises it as soon as it has
+         * retired the descriptor - so spin for the first rounds; once it
+         * has still not arrived, stop burning the core and poll at the OS
+         * tick instead.  The budget is rounds plus naps, a real time
+         * bound, rather than an iteration count whose duration is whatever
+         * the compiler made of the loop.
+         */
+        volatile uint32_t spins = 0;
+        volatile uint32_t naps = 0;
         while (qh->killed != 2) {
-            timeout++;
-            if (timeout > 200000U) {
-                /* The iaad was consumed before killed went to 1, so no
-                 * interrupt will ever finish the handshake. If the slot
-                 * still belongs to this urb the kill owns the completion;
-                 * if a concurrent completion already finished the urb,
-                 * touching the slot again would double-free it. */
-                flags = usb_osal_enter_critical_section();
-                bool orphan = (qh->inuse && qh->urb == urb && urb->hcpriv == qh);
-                qh->remove_in_iaad = 0;
-                qh->killed = 0;
-                usb_osal_leave_critical_section(flags);
-                if (!orphan) {
-                    return -USB_ERR_TIMEOUT;
+            if (++spins > 1000U) {
+                if (++naps > 200U) {
+                    /* The iaad was consumed before killed went to 1, so no
+                     * interrupt will ever finish the handshake. If the slot
+                     * still belongs to this urb the kill owns the completion;
+                     * if a concurrent completion already finished the urb,
+                     * touching the slot again would double-free it. */
+                    flags = usb_osal_enter_critical_section();
+                    bool orphan = (qh->inuse && qh->urb == urb && urb->hcpriv == qh);
+                    qh->remove_in_iaad = 0;
+                    qh->killed = 0;
+                    usb_osal_leave_critical_section(flags);
+                    if (!orphan) {
+                        return -USB_ERR_TIMEOUT;
+                    }
+                    break;
                 }
-                break;
+                usb_osal_msleep(1);
             }
         }
     } else {
-- 
